      "message": "[error] Line 27: 🔴 The cached `Call.resolvedSystemConnection` is never invalidated when a resolved Telecom connection terminates or is rejected. After `PendingIncomingCall` removes its generation, a later RINGING/retry returns this disposed `AndroidCall` instead of creating a new request; notification setup then waits on a completed connection and no new Telecom UI is created. Clear/invalidate the call\u0027s cached connection on termination, or only reuse it while its live registry entry remains valid, and add a retry-after-connection-termination test.",
